widget and in external editors over LSP, with key, value, [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]punctuation, literal type, and declaration validity each visually [/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]         [#D7D7AF][/dim]distinct and driven by one shared Rust grammar.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim] Counts: [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]5[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] phases[dim][/dim] · [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]3[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] waves[/dim]\n[dim]   Path: [#87AFFF][/dim]plan:202609/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]xprompt_keyword_arg_highlighting.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim] Prompt: [#87AFFF][/dim]prompts/202609/xprompt_keyword_arg_highlighting.md[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Bead: [#87AFFF][/dim]sase-11i[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Page: [#87AFFF][/dim]https://github.com/sase-org/sase--beads/blob/main/pages/sase-11i/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]README.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Argument span grammar in the Rust core[/bold #D7AFFF]                        [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]core-spans[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]core-spans: add a frontend-neutral xprompt/directive argument span [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]tokenizer to sase-core that decomposes every argument form into key, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]assign, value, and delimiter roles with literal-type and validity [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]classification, and stop treating unresolvable values as type [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]mismatches.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]LSP semantic tokens for argument structure[/bold #D7AFFF]                    [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]lsp-tokens[dim] · [dim][/dim]after core-spans[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]lsp-tokens: grow the xprompt LSP semantic token legend with standard LSP[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]token types and emit argument-structure tokens from the core spans, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]merged against the existing artifact, code, and glossary tokens.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Neovim legend safety and default highlight links[/bold #D7AFFF]              [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]nvim-groups[dim] · [dim][/dim]after lsp-tokens[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]nvim-groups: make the glossary underline filter legend-proof, add [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]default highlight links only where a standard token type reads poorly on[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]a plain colorscheme, and cover the new tokens with an LSP smoke test.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]ACE prompt widget argument rendering[/bold #D7AFFF]                          [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]tui-render[dim] · [dim][/dim]after core-spans[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]tui-render: consume the core spans in the prompt text area and the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]shared span partition, add the new highlight roles and their theme ramp,[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]and stop the argument container role from overpainting nested Jinja, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]placeholder, and artifact spans.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Visual snapshots and cross-surface parity[/bold #D7AFFF]                     [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]visual-parity[dim] · [dim][/dim]after lsp-tokens, tui-render[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]visual-parity: pin the new rendering with dark and light PNG snapshots, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]prove the TUI and LSP classify the same text identically, and confirm [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the CLI and pager surfaces render every new role.[/#D7D7AF]","clan_tribe":"epic","epic_bead_id":"sase-11i","llm_provider":"codex","model":"gpt-5.5","patch_name":"gh_sase-org__sase","phase_bead_id":"sase-11i.1","reasoning_effort":"xh